 "kit": "A Briar Guard, heavy infantry: thick armour of black-brown bark plates studded with short thorns on the shoulders, arms and legs; a sleeveless surcoat of deep bottle-green cloth that covers his whole chest and belly from the collar down to just below the knees, front and back, split at the front below the belt so the legs can stride and held at the waist by a thorn-studded belt, worn over the bark plates of the body; a closed bark helm crowned with a ring of thorns and a deep green leaf crest; a heavy deep bottle-green mantle across the shoulders and the upper back; a long halberd with a curved thorn-shaped blade, a back hook and a spike. No shield, no antlers. Big and broad.",
